---
// Privacy Policy (EN). Written for the new site following the Xana standard
// publication protocol (GDPR/LOPDGDD structure): the previous WordPress page
// only carried the CMS boilerplate. The "Data Deletion Policy" for the App
// Catalog Platform is carried over verbatim (required by the Play Store).
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { COMPANY, LEGAL_ROUTES } from '../i18n/content';
const alternates = { en: LEGAL_ROUTES.en.privacy, es: LEGAL_ROUTES.es.privacy };
---

<Legal
  locale="en"
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Xana Technologies SL processes the personal data collected through xanatechnologies.com: purposes, legal basis, recipients, retention and your rights."
  alternates={alternates}
  updated="9 September 2026"
>
  <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Controller:</strong> {COMPANY.legalName} (Tax ID {COMPANY.taxId})</li>
    <li><strong>Registered office:</strong> {COMPANY.addressEn}</li>
    <li><strong>Privacy contact:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a></li>
    <li><strong>Website:</strong> <a href={COMPANY.website}>xanatechnologies.com</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    {COMPANY.legalName} processes personal data in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR)
    and Spanish Organic Law 3/2018 on the Protection of Personal Data and guarantee of digital rights
    (LOPDGDD). We only process personal data when there is a valid legal basis to do so.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What data we process, why and on what basis</h2>
  <div class="legal-table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Processing</th><th>Data</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis</th><th>Retention</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Contact form</td>
          <td>Email address and message (required); name, phone, region and country (optional); language; IP address for anti-bot verification.</td>
          <td>To answer your enquiry and, where relevant, route it to the appropriate brand (Xana System or Woman on Mars) or prepare a proposal.</td>
          <td>Your consent (GDPR art. 6.1.a) and pre-contractual measures taken at your request (art. 6.1.b).</td>
          <td>For as long as needed to handle the enquiry and, afterwards, for the period required to meet legal obligations or defend possible claims.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Commercial relationship</td>
          <td>Identification and contact details of clients, partners and their representatives.</td>
          <td>To manage the commercial and contractual relationship.</td>
          <td>Performance of a contract (art. 6.1.b) and legitimate interest (art. 6.1.f).</td>
          <td>For the duration of the relationship and the legal limitation periods thereafter.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Website analytics</td>
          <td>Pseudonymous usage data collected through cookies (see the Cookies Policy).</td>
          <td>To measure how the site is used and improve it.</td>
          <td>Your consent, given through the cookie banner (art. 6.1.a).</td>
          <td>See the cookie durations in the Cookies Policy.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Providing the data marked as required in the contact form is necessary to handle your enquiry;
    without it we cannot reply. We do not use your data for automated decision-making or profiling.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Recipients</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell your personal data. It may be processed by service providers acting on our behalf
    as data processors, under data processing agreements, in the following categories:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Hosting and delivery of the website and contact form:</strong> Vercel Inc.</li>
    <li><strong>Transactional email of the contact form:</strong> Brevo (Sendinblue SAS).</li>
    <li><strong>Anti-bot verification of the contact form:</strong> Cloudflare, Inc. (Turnstile).</li>
    <li><strong>Website analytics (only with your consent):</strong> Google Ireland Ltd. (Google Tag Manager, Google Analytics).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Data may also be disclosed to public authorities or other third parties when there is a legal
    obligation or another valid legal basis to do so.
  </p>

  <h2>4. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Some of the providers listed above may process data outside the European Economic Area (in
    particular in the United States). Where that happens, transfers are covered by the safeguards
    required by the GDPR: an adequacy decision of the European Commission (including the EU-U.S.
    Data Privacy Framework, where the provider is certified) and/or the Standard Contractual Clauses
    approved by the Commission.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Data is kept only for as long as necessary for the purposes stated above and, afterwards, for
    the periods required to comply with legal obligations or to address possible liabilities, after
    which it is securely deleted.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You may request, at any time:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access to your personal data;</li>
    <li>rectification of inaccurate data;</li>
    <li>erasure;</li>
    <li>restriction of processing;</li>
    <li>data portability;</li>
    <li>objection to processing;</li>
    <li>withdrawal of consent, without affecting the lawfulness of processing carried out before withdrawal.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise these rights, write to <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> or to
    our registered office, indicating the right you wish to exercise and enclosing a copy of a valid
    identity document. You may also lodge a complaint with the competent supervisory authority, the
    Spanish Data Protection Agency (AEPD, <a href="https://www.aepd.es" rel="noopener" target="_blank">www.aepd.es</a>).
  </p>

  <h2>7. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We apply appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect your personal data against
    unauthorised access, alteration, disclosure or loss, taking into account the state of the art
    and the risks of the processing.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Information about the cookies and similar technologies used on this website is available in our
    <a href={LEGAL_ROUTES.en.cookies}>Cookies Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Data Deletion Policy (App Catalog Platform)</h2>
  <p>
    This account deletion policy applies to the App Catalog Platform application, developed by Xana
    Technologies and available on the Play Store.
  </p>
  <p>Users may request deletion of their accounts by following these steps:</p>
  <ol type="a">
    <li>Send an email to <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> with the subject line “Account Deletion.” You must include the email address used to register.</li>
    <li>Within 7–10 days, the company will contact you to confirm the deletion of your data from the system.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>All account data will be deleted. No records will be retained.</p>
  <p>
    Please note that this policy is subject to periodic changes and updates. Users are encouraged to
    review this policy regularly to stay informed of any modifications. For any questions or requests
    related to this policy, please do not hesitate to contact us.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy when necessary. Any changes will be published on this page with
    an updated revision date. Privacy contact:
    <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
